  "findings": [
    "All 135 underbarrel actions across 27 weapon roots link through secondary selector object GUIDs to parts listed in the parent WB. There are 393 one-selector matches, not 393 fully evaluated activations.",
    "Each M320 family has base, Plus and Reload parts; M26DB has base and Reload parts. Plus parts also list the Grenadier_Base selector; Reload parts also list AssaultGadgetReload. Exact selectors are retained for native condition review.",
    "All four Plus effects share their complete scalar fields, including Field_7f22bfb4=30 and Field_4614adfe=6. All five Reload effects have Field_348b8cd1=1.1. These are serialized operands, not measured ammunition counts or timing gains.",
    "HK417A2, M4A1 and XM7 each have one inline Generic part with Class_4aac041b Field_9540bd8e=1. All 15 references to that selector match.",
    "All 40 unmatched references are U_WPM_UBL_Any in the checked parent WB part lists; this does not prove global non-use.",
    "M26DB includes an internal firing object with a buckshot projectile reference and a separate Class_b1afeb65 effect that references Dragonbreath with priority 9000. Native application remains unverified."
  ],
  "supersedes": "The earlier additional-ubl-primary-branch-joins-draft.json zero-WPM counts only inspected Field_7e54e22c. They cannot describe all underbarrel modifier links.",
  "limits": "Exact serialized joins and reachable part contents only. Secondary list application, SRU semantics, condition evaluation and runtime switching remain open. Fresh target resolution does not fully review target fields. Layout warnings are retained. One matching selector does not satisfy every selector on a part. No whole-asset semantic closure, runtime behavior, inventory count or timing percentage is established."
}
